{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779718847,"nonce":"n730ug1K9KKvvH5MxKvY5on8g5I=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDUSK8g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/171","origin":"github"},"title":"Operator annunciator misses battery/LVD, sound-speed, and FCU-error status (gaps from 2026-05-22)","message":"## Context\nCross-checking the 2026-05-22 diagnostics (analysis in #169, §8) against what the **operator annunciator** actually displayed: several real ERROR/degraded conditions never surfaced to the operator. The operator config (`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_operator_annunciator.yaml`) currently has **only network/link indicators** (WiFi, Starlink, pings, UDP bridge) — no battery, sound-speed, or FCU-system indicators. The boat config (`bizzyboat_annunciator.yaml`) has Battery/GPS/FCU but with the gaps below.\n\nThis was a deliberate drain-to-LVD test, so the operator's annunciator showed only comms status and gave **no battery warning** as the pack fell to 21.2 V, no SV-failure indication, and no FCU-error indication. For autonomous / over-horizon ops the annunciator is the operator's primary health view — these are safety-relevant coverage gaps.\n\n## Gaps to fix\n\n- [ ] **No sound-speed indicator.** `sound_speed_bridge` was in ERROR for the *entire* deployment (SV never delivered — see #163), but neither annunciator has a sound-speed indicator. → add a `sound_speed_bridge` indicator (boat + operator).\n\n- [ ] **Battery never went yellow/red despite draining to LVD.** The operator annunciator has **no battery indicator at all**. The boat annunciator's `Battery` indicator keys on the `mavros: Battery` diagnostic *level*, which stayed OK throughout — the low-voltage condition actually surfaced on `mavros: System` (\"FCU: Battery 1 is low 22.88V\"), and `mavros: Battery` doesn't threshold on voltage because the FCU battery monitor is unconfigured (no current meter; `percentage` = −0.01, \"used 0 mAh\"). → add a battery indicator to the **operator** annunciator and threshold on the **voltage value** (the engine supports value-threshold expressions — cf. `rqt_annunciator/test/test_threshold.py`) rather than the diagnostic level. Suggest WARN/ERROR voltage thresholds tuned to the Torqeedo Power 24-3500 pack (e.g. ~22.5 / 21.5 V — tune).\n\n- [ ] **FCU / `mavros: System` errors don't reach the operator.** `mavros: System` carried 4,597 ERROR msgs (the low-battery failsafe among them) but isn't on the operator annunciator (operator config has no FCU indicator; boat config surfaces only `mavros: Heartbeat` as \"FCU\" and `mavros: GPS`). → add a `mavros: System` indicator to the operator annunciator.\n\n## Scope\nConfig only — `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_operator_annunciator.yaml` (+ `bizzyboat_annunciator.yaml` for the SV indicator). The `rqt_annunciator` engine (rolker/rqt_operator_tools) already supports diagnostic-name matching and value thresholds; no code change expected. Confirm the battery voltage is exposed as a KeyValue on a diagnostic the annunciator reads (e.g. `mavros: Battery`'s Voltage field).\n\n## References\n- Surfaced in #169 (§8 diagnostics cross-check); sound velocity #163.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}